### Compass client configuration — AC-21, AC-22, AC-23
###
### Every route requires the Compass Super Admin policy. A "Compass Admin" principal is refused with
### 403 on ALL of these, reads included — that role is read-only in Compass however administrative the
### name sounds (AC-44, FR-028).
###
### Locally, `make dev-all` runs DevBypass, so requests are already authenticated. Confirm you actually
### hold the role before blaming a 403:
###   curl -s http://localhost:5009/api/me | jq '.privileges'
### If "Compass Super Admin" is missing, fix the bypass principal's groups. Do NOT relax a policy to
### make a request work.
###
### ⚠️ THERE IS NO CLIENT STATUS, IN EITHER DIRECTION.
### A client's Active/Inactive is DERIVED from its assignments (FR-021, FR-035) — never stored, never
### settable, and absent from every payload below. A request carrying one is REJECTED with 400 rather
### than ignored: the request records opt into JsonUnmappedMemberHandling.Disallow, because silently
### discarding "isActive": false would answer 201 to someone who believes they just deactivated a
### client. See the deliberate-400 request at the bottom of this file.
###
### There is deliberately NO DELETE, for clients or categories. A category is retired by PUTting
### isActive false (AC-23); a client is never retired at all, because its status is derived.
###
### Every write here IS audited, and the audited scope INCLUDES the billable time categories and the
### invoice-frequency default (AC-NFR-3, verbatim). Category changes are attributed to the CLIENT's
### record, so one query answers "what changed about this client":
###   curl -s "http://localhost:5009/api/audit-logs?entityType=CompassClient" | jq '.[0]'

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5009
@clients = {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/clients

### Every client, ordered by name. The invoice-frequency default is resolved to its NAME here (the
### list renders it); the full record below carries the id instead, because the form populates its own
### select from the active-only lookup list.
GET {{clients}}

### One client's full record, including every billable time category — active AND inactive. Inactive
### ones are included on purpose: an administrator who cannot see a retired category cannot reactivate
### one.
GET {{clients}}/1

### Add a client. Note what is NOT here: any status member.
### The invoice-frequency default is optional; when supplied it must name an ACTIVE type, which the
### server enforces even though the selection list omits inactive ones (FR-023, FR-041).
POST {{clients}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Contoso",
  "msaSignedDate": "2024-03-01",
  "ndaSignedDate": "2024-02-14",
  "isInternal": false,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": 1
}

### A client with no contract dates and no cadence. All three are optional — this is an ordinary
### client, not an incomplete one, and it is immediately available for assignment at zero assignments
### (FR-022).
POST {{clients}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Fabrikam",
  "msaSignedDate": null,
  "ndaSignedDate": null,
  "isInternal": false,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": null
}

### An internal EDJE client. The "beach" flag — an assignment to a client with this set is what the
### dashboard's "on the beach" tile counts.
POST {{clients}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Leading EDJE — Internal",
  "msaSignedDate": null,
  "ndaSignedDate": null,
  "isInternal": true,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": null
}

### 409 — the client name is already in use. The pre-check names the field; the real guard is
### ux_client_client_name, so a caller who LOSES a concurrent race gets this same 409 rather than a 500.
POST {{clients}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Contoso",
  "msaSignedDate": null,
  "ndaSignedDate": null,
  "isInternal": false,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": null
}

### 400 — the invoice frequency is unknown OR retired. One question, not two: the answer is the same
### either way. Retire a cadence via PUT /api/compass/v1/admin/invoice-frequency-types/{id} and retry.
POST {{clients}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Northwind",
  "msaSignedDate": null,
  "ndaSignedDate": null,
  "isInternal": false,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": 999999
}

### Update a client. An edit that LEAVES an already-set but since-retired cadence alone is accepted
### (FR-007: retiring a lookup value must not rewrite records already using it); MOVING to a different
### retired one is refused.
PUT {{clients}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Contoso",
  "msaSignedDate": "2024-03-01",
  "ndaSignedDate": "2024-02-14",
  "isInternal": true,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": 1
}

### Add a billable time category. Names are unique PER CLIENT, not globally — two clients may both
### offer "Development", and that is the ordinary case rather than the exceptional one (FR-025, FR-006).
POST {{clients}}/1/billable-time-categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryName": "Development"
}

### 409 — this client already offers that name. Try the same request against a DIFFERENT client id and
### it succeeds; that difference is the whole rule.
POST {{clients}}/1/billable-time-categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryName": "Development"
}

### Retire a category. This is the ONLY retirement path — there is no DELETE (AC-23, Principle VIII).
### The row stays, keeps its name, and keeps its client; timesheet records referencing it are untouched.
PUT {{clients}}/1/billable-time-categories/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryName": "Development",
  "isActive": false
}

### 404 — the category exists but belongs to a DIFFERENT client. The client id is part of the lookup,
### not a hint, so guessing an id cannot reach someone else's configuration.
PUT {{clients}}/2/billable-time-categories/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryName": "Renamed",
  "isActive": true
}

### 400 — DELIBERATE. This is FR-021's inbound half, and the thing most worth trying by hand: a request
### that tries to set a client's status is REFUSED, not silently ignored. Change "isActive" to any
### unmapped member and the answer is the same 400.
POST {{clients}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Statusful Corp",
  "msaSignedDate": null,
  "ndaSignedDate": null,
  "isInternal": false,
  "invoiceFrequencyTypeId": null,
  "isActive": false
}
